[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find the minimum value of the sum of distances from a point \(X\) to the vertices of the pentagon \(ABCDE\), i.e., \(f(X) = AX + BX + CX + DX + EX\). This problem is related to the Fermat point of the pentagon, which minimizes the sum of distances to its vertices.
