[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m First, we will consider the triangle \(BCE\). Since \( \angle B = \angle E = 60^\circ \), the triangle \(BCE\) can be divided into two \(60^\circ\) angles and a smaller triangle by adding a point \(Y\) inside the triangle such that \( \angle BYE = 120^\circ \).
