[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m Let $ABCDE$ be a convex pentagon with $AB=14$, $BC=7$, $CD=24$, $DE=13$, $EA=26$, and $\angle B=\angle E=60^{\circ}$. For each point $X$ in the plane, define $f(X)=AX+BX+CX+DX+EX$. The least possible value of $f(X)$ can be expressed as $m+n\sqrt{p}$, where $m$ and $n$ are positive integers and $p$ is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find $m+n+p$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
