[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m The minimum value of \( f(X) \) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m \[ f(X) = AB + BC + CD + DE + EA = 14 + 7 + 24 + 13 + 26 = 84. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m However, we need to consider the fact that the Fermat point minimizes the sum of the distances, and the minimum value is actually the sum of the sides of the pentagon minus the length of the segment connecting the Fermat point to the vertices of the pentagon. The length of this segment is the length of the equilateral triangle formed by the sides of the pentagon.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
