[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m So, the least possible value of \( f(X) \) is \( 84 - 26\sqrt{3} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m The value \( 84 - 26\sqrt{3} \) can be expressed as \( m + n\sqrt{p} \) where \( m = 84 \), \( n = -26 \), and \( p = 3 \). Since \( m \) and \( n \) are positive integers, we take the absolute value of \( n \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
