[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m In our case, the disk can be considered as a plane, and we are adding line segments that intersect the disk. Initially, there are 4 regions formed by the two perpendicular diameters (which divide the disk into 4 quadrants). We then add 25 more line segments, making a total of 27 line segments.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m The formula for the maximum number of regions that \( n \) lines can divide a plane into is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=439428)[0m \[
